(a) Connection and/or dedication entirely discretionary. As the operation, maintenance, repair and replacement of the public sanitary sewer is a municipal service provided to the residents of the city and the rate payers, all applications for expansion or modification of the existing underground public infrastructure is governed by the capacity available through the city's existing facilities. For this reason, the city reserves approval to the water and sewer director who shall possess the discretion to accept or deny any modification or expansion of the existing public sanitary sewer, and same shall only be made in writing.
(b) Any application for real estate development to expand or modify the existing public sanitary sewer using a lift station to generate mechanical flow for sewage shall provide clear and convincing evidence that use of natural gravity flow is not feasible due to the conditions of geography and topography, and fiscal cost alone shall not the determinative factor for feasibility.
(c) Any application submitted for the use of a sanitary lift station in the public sanitary sewer shall meet the following specifications to be eligible for consideration:
(1) The proposed sanitary lift station shall be designed by a professional engineer, licensed by the State of Georgia, and shall be designed and constructed in accordance with the adopted Calhoun Utilities Development Policies and Specifications for Water and Sanitary Sewer in effect at the time of the application;
(2) The proposed sanitary lift station shall deliver a minimum mechanical flow rate of not less than 200 gallons per minute and serve the largest watershed sub-basin feasible;
(3) The proposed sanitary lift station shall provide a minimum area of public sanitary sewer service for an area not less than the equivalent of one square mile of land whether occupied entirely by the real estate development;
(4) The real estate development, if not located geographically within the existing boundaries of the city at the time of application, must be located at or beyond the nearest downstream confluence outside the proposed development, and shall lie geographically within one linear mile of the then existing municipal boundary;
(5) The proposed sanitary lift station shall support the expected flow rates, volume of sanitary sewage waste, and system capacity required for not less than 300 EDU connections to be considered;
(6) The proposal cannot locate the new sanitary lift station upstream of an existing sanitary lift station; and only gravity flow shall be permitted to transport sewage to the existing lift station without mechanical intervention;
(7) The proposal cannot locate the new sanitary lift station downstream of an existing sanitary lift station with the expectation that this "chain" shall reach a point for gravity flow in the public sanitary sewer, and only gravity flow shall be used to transport sewage to the existing lift station for new or expanded service; and
(8) All other conditions or requirements that may be enacted by the periodic modification of the Calhoun Utilities Development Policies and Specifications for Water and Sanitary Sewer.
(d) All sanitary sewer availability requests for land outside of the city's geographical limits shall be subject to approval by the governing authority upon the recommendation of the utilities administrator, and should the proposed parcel of real property meet all statutory requirements, the owner or developer shall be required to request annexation of the subject territory.
(e) If an application under consideration is to be granted, the municipal engineer shall first have approved the proposed location and final design before construction shall begin.
(Ord. No. 2018, Exh. A, 6-8-2026)

